Z||000002||Songman||08-09-2001||11:25 AM||||I'd go to court over a picture of my car supposedly speeding. First off, I may not have even been driving the car. Second, a picture of a car doesn't prove you are speeding..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||08-09-2001||11:52 AM||||Just like the red light cams, it doesn't matter if it was you driving or not. If someone borrows your car and runs a red light, YOU get the citation. Their mindset is that you shouldn't have loaned your car to someone who was going to use it irresponsibly.<P>What a crock of $hit. I'm getting real damn tired of the way traffic enforcement is handled these days. I'm going to start a GD class-action suit for harassment against the whole damn police force because they make me feel like I'm going to get pulled over for some BS even when I'm not doing anything wrong. It pi$$es me off to feel like I have to walk on eggshells for no damn reason whatsoever. I'm a good driver, and a safe one. SO LEAVE ME THE F ALONE. If you see me breaking the law, nail my ass. But until you do, F off.||||reg||1
