Z||000017||FieroKyle||08-09-2001||09:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>Just like the red light cams, it doesn't matter if it was you driving or not. If someone borrows your car and runs a red light, YOU get the citation. Their mindset is that you shouldn't have loaned your car to someone who was going to use it irresponsibly.<P>What a crock of $hit. I'm getting real damn tired of the way traffic enforcement is handled these days. I'm going to start a GD class-action suit for harassment against the whole damn police force because they make me feel like I'm going to get pulled over for some BS even when I'm not doing anything wrong. It pi$$es me off to feel like I have to walk on eggshells for no damn reason whatsoever. I'm a good driver, and a safe one. SO LEAVE ME THE F ALONE. If you see me breaking the law, nail my ass. But until you do, F off.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I feel like the same thing. I passed a cop on the expressway doing the speedlimit and he had the gun point right at me. I felt like he was gonna pull me over for stupid bullshit. And the thing is he just held it on my car. At first I didn't know it was a cop because is was a chevy astro, then I see the side with county stickers on it. Its a bunch of BS anymore.<BR>||||reg||1
